### 🧠 Summary & Advice

| ✅ Do | ❌ Don’t |
|------|--------|
| Keep track of timeout/times out manually. | Expect `set()->read()->set()` to be idempotent across libuv cycles. |
| Use `with_net_buffer()` to **retain** control, then call `worker.sleep()` or `wait()` after clearing. | Treat `wakeup.wait` as a one-time operation. |
| Consider polling with `with_net_buffer()` and manage backoff yourself. | Assume libuv exposes dynamic API for `SO_RCVTIMEO`. |

